Description: 2D CAD drafting application with native DXF and DWG support
 LyCAD is a 2D CAD drafting application written in C++20 with Qt 6 and CMake.
 DXF and DWG are handled by code compiled into the binary itself (a modified
 libdxfrw for reading, a built-in writer for DWG output), so no external
 converter, command line tool or library package is needed at run time.
 .
 The drawing model covers lines, arcs, circles, ellipses, polylines, splines,
 hatches, text and multi-line text with inline formatting, blocks and insert
 references, dimensions, tables and lights. Editing provides object snapping
 with per-snap priority, ortho and polar tracking, grip editing, undo/redo and
 a command line, with a ribbon UI in light and dark themes.
 .
 DWG can be written in the AutoCAD 2000 through 2018 formats (R2000 - R2018).
